      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For standard dark chocolate, the melting phase should gently bring the chocolate up to around 110-120°F (43-49°C). Next, you must cool the melted chocolate down to the seeding temperature, typically between 86-88°F (30-31°C), to encourage the formation of stable Form V crystals. Finally, reheat the mixture slightly to around 88-91°F (31-33°C) to ensure all unwanted, unstable crystals melt away, leaving only the perfect structure.",
